  "A samurai with a rank between goshi and joshi. This rank was exclusively bestowed to Tosa Domain goshi and their families for notable achievements.": "上級武士である上士と\n下級武士である郷士の間に位置する階級。",
  "The process of reformation and rebirth, restoration, or revolution.": "世の中の様々なことが改革され、新しくなること。",
  "A term used to refer to European countries, often Portugal. [Nanban as a term originated from the Chinese term referring to those of the south, such as the current South East Asian countries. This term was borrowed by the Japanese, and eventually included the Portuguese and other Europeans, and started being used as a term for those that came from outside of Japan.] ": "主にポルトガルなどの\nヨーロッパ諸国を指す言葉。",
  "Kyo ": "京",
  "The northeast region of Kyo. Became known as the Fushimi Ward after the city was renamed \"Kyoto.\"": "京の南部に位置する地域。",
  "The area lying within Kyo's city limits.": "京の市中の地域を指す。",
  "The suburban area surrounding Kyo, not counting the city itself.": "京の郊外の地域を指す。",
  "A shopping and entertainment district with bustling streets typical to Kyo.": "京都市東山区にある、\n京都の代表的な繁華街及び歓楽街。",
  "Aizu Domain": "会津藩",
  "A domain located in the northeast of Honshu. The area is part of the current-day Fukushima Prefecture.": "会津郡（現在の福島県にあった郡）を\n中心とした地域を統治していた組織。",
  "A sword that is over 90 centimeters (nearly three feet) in length.": "刃渡りが約９０ｃｍ以上ある大型の刀の事。",
  "A sword that is between between 30 and 60 centimeters (around one to two feet) in length. ": "刃渡り３０ｃｍから６０ｃｍぐらいの刀の事。",
  "Seppuku": "切腹",
  "Loyalist": "勤王",
  "Nanki": "南紀派",
  "Nanban ": "南蛮",
  "Doshin": "同心",
  "A traditional Japanese overcoat, normally hip- or waist-length. Once only worn by the warrior classes, the Edo period saw some commoners starting to wear haori to formal occasions as well.": "和服における上着の一種。\n防寒、おしゃれを目的として着る。",
  "A domain in Shikoku, north of the Tosa Domain. The area is part of the current-day Ehime Prefecture.": "土佐に対して北に位置する、四国の一部。",
  "A province northeast of Tosa. The area is part of the current-day Tokushima Prefecture.": "土佐の北東に隣接する地域で、徳島藩の一部。",
  "\"Sonno\" is a declaration that the foremost leader of the nation is the Emperor, as opposed to the Bakufu.\n\n\"Joui\" is a demand to drive out all foreigners and refuse them access to the nation.": "外敵を撃ち払って入国させないこと。 \n外国人を追い払って通交しないこと。",
  "Ozu": "大洲",
  "Tairo": "大老",
  "Tenchu": "天誅",
  "Okami ": "女将",
  "Ansei Purge": "安政の大獄",
  "Heir": "宗家",
  "An adult son who is ineligible to inherit his family's title, yet continues to live in his parents' house without attaining independence. ": "家督を相続できない子孫が、\n独立せずに親の家に住んでいる状態のこと。",
  "Sun / Shaku": "寸／尺",
  "Koban": "小判",
  "Kodachi ": "小太刀",
  "Kodachi Handling ": "小太刀術",
  "A domain encompassing much of Shikoku's southern region, ruled by the Yamauchi clan. The area is now known as the Kochi Prefecture.": "山内氏が支配する、\n四国の南に位置する大藩。",
  "Shrine Maiden ": "巫女",
  "A lower-ranking Bakufu official typically assigned to law enforcement. Employed by the various officials of Kyo, they were in charge of policing the majority of the city's criminal activity.": "幕府の下級役人の一つ。\n諸奉行、京都所司代などに属し、町の犯罪者の\n取り締まりなどを担当する。",
  "A political group founded in the Tosa Domain near the end of the Edo period.": "幕末の土佐（現在の高知県）に存在した、政治結社。",
  "A term of respect for a woman running her own business. ": "店の長が女性の場合の呼称。",
  "A top-level Bakufu officer permitted direct contact with the Shogun. In the Sengoku period, they were the samurai serving as the closest bodyguards for their lords. By the Edo period, they were given a much wider range of duties and were often awarded land. ": "徳川家直属の家臣で\n将軍に直接会うことを許された者の総称。",
  "Three Houses of the Tokugawa": "徳川御三家",
  "The three Tokugawa family clans of highest nobility and the only heirs permitted to claim the Tokugawa name. They consist of the Owari, the Kishu, and the Mito clans, each ruling over their namesake domains.": "徳川氏の中で、将軍家に次ぐ家で\n徳川姓を名乗ることを許された家。\n尾張徳川家、紀州徳川家、水戸徳川家の３つの家のこと。",
  "Shishi": "志士",
  "Ebisu": "恵比寿様",
  "An action taken by someone who believes they are fulfilling the will of the heavens as a form of \"divine punishment.\"": "悪行を行った人間を制裁すること。",
  "Sengoku Period": "戦国/戦国時代",
  "A clan of samurai led by their namesake lord who united the Shikoku lands during the Sengoku period. When the Yamauchi clan was granted the Tosa domain, many former Chosokabe samurai were appointed the rank of goshi, while the samurai under Yamauchi were appointed the rank of joshi.": "戦国時代、土佐を中心に四国で活躍した大名。",
  "A person residing in a domain besides their own. While the term is regularly used with samurai, it is not exclusive to their class.": "所属していた藩から離れて生活している人のこと。\nそのため侍であるとは限らない。",
  "The military government led by the Shogun. Often referred to as \"the shogunate\" in Western writing.": "政治を行う場所。政府。",
  "Mon / Ryo": "文／両",
  "Hatamoto": "旗本",
  "Mechanical contraptions built using historic engineering methods.": "日本における古い時代の機械的仕組みのこと。",
  "Equivalent to a pub, it is a bar that serves a variety of food as well.": "日本における飲み屋。酒類と料理を提供する飲食店。\n日本版のバーやパブといった店である。",
  "Traditional Japanese underwear. Comprised of a strip of cloth connected to a waist strap so that the wearer must step into the leg holes to don the underwear.": "日本の伝統的な下着。\n基本的には帯状の布に腰ひもがついた形状。",
  "A sweet beverage typically made from fermented rice. The alcohol content can range from low to none, depending on production methods.": "日本の伝統的な甘味飲料。\n主に米や米を醗酵したものを原料にする。",
  "One of the Seven Gods of Fortune in Japanese culture. He is typically depicted with a fishing rod in his right hand and a sea bream tucked under his left arm.": "日本の神。七福神の一柱。\n右手に釣り竿を持ち、左脇に鯛を抱える姿が一般的。",
  "A war-torn era of Japan's history that began in the late 15th century and lasted well over a hundred years.": "日本国内で１５世紀末から１６世紀末にかけて\n戦乱が頻発した時代のこと。",
  "A high-end restaurant that serves classical Japanese cuisine. They usually have a restricted clientele list, accepting new customers by referral only.": "日本料理を提供する、高級飲食店のこと。",
  "A major city in central Japan, later renamed \"Tokyo.\" It was already one of the largest metropolises in the world by the end of the Edo period.": "東京中心部の場所を指す。",
  "Sakurada Gate": "桜田門",
  "Sukhavati ": "極楽浄土",
  "The act of samurai cutting down passersby on the streets, in order to test the sharpness of their blades. Basically street murder. ": "武士が刀の切れ味を試すため、路上で行きずりの\n人を斬る行為。",
  "A high-ranking samurai.": "武士の中でも上位階級の者のこと。",
  "A low-ranking samurai.": "武士の中でも下級の者のこと。",
  "A place to practice martial arts. ": "武術の修練を行う施設。",
  "Mito Domain": "水戸藩",
  "Edo": "江戸",
  "One of the innermost gates protecting Edo Castle and the site of Ii Naosuke's assassination at the hands of ronin samurai.": "江戸城の内堀に造られた門の一つ。",
  "A red-light district officially sanctioned by the Edo Bakufu.": "江戸幕府によって公認された遊郭。",
  "The highest position grantable in the Bakufu. They worked closely with their appointing Shoguns, and would even take over as temporary leaders in times where the Shogun could not serve.": "江戸幕府の職名。将軍の補佐役であり最高職である。",
  "An oval-shaped gold coin used throughout the Edo period. Despite their size shrinking over the centuries, they kept a consistent exchange rate of one ryo to one koban until their use was discontinued.": "江戸時代に作られ使用された金貨。\n楕円形で、基本的に１両の価値があった。",
  "Units of measurement commonly used in Japan during the Edo period. 1 shaku = 10 sun = ~30.3 centimeters (~11.93 inches).": "江戸時代に日本で採用されていた、長さの単位。\n１尺＝１０寸＝３０．３ｃｍ（１１．９３ｉｎ）",
  "A samurai's self-exile from his domain, with punishment for returning potentially including death. ": "江戸時代に武士が所属していた\n藩（国や地域組織）を出ていく（やめる）事。",
  "A social movement during the late Edo period where commoners created seemingly-pointless public disturbances. Crowds would parade through town, dancing and chanting \"Ee ja nai ka\" (roughly translating to \"Why not?\" or \"Who cares?\"). Some believe this was a form of protest, but no explicit purpose has ever been discovered. These incidents sometimes resulted in nearby crimes of opportunity, such as burglary.": "江戸時代の末期、\n主に江戸（現在の東京）より西の地域で起こった騒動。\n民衆が“ええじゃないか”と叫び集団で町や村を練り歩いた。\n地主や商人たちの屋敷に入り込んで物品などを強要、\n強奪するような事件が相次いだ。",
  "Currency used in Japan during the Edo period. The exchange rate for ryo (gold coins) and mon (silver coins) fluctuated daily. By the end of the period, the prevailing market rate was over 8,000 mon for a single ryo.": "江戸時代の通貨単位。\n両（金貨）、文（銀貨）の交換レートは毎日変動した。\n幕末の実勢相場は１両が８０００文を上回る状況だった。",
  "Uraga": "浦賀",
  "An individual or like-minded group who is loyal first and foremost to the Emperor of Japan.": "王や天皇に忠義を尽くすこと。",
  "Currently named \"Kyoto,\" this was the city where the nation's Emperors held residence for nearly eleven centuries.": "現在の京都の事。帝の住まいのある地域の事を指す。\n江戸時代は現在の京都にあった。",
  "A domain located in the southwest of Honshu. The area is part of the current-day Yamaguchi Prefecture.": "現在の山口県を中心とした地域を統治していた組織。",
  "A port town located where the Uraga Channel meets the Tokyo Bay. The area is now part of Yokosuka, in the current-day Kanagawa Prefecture.": "現在の神奈川県横須賀市東部にある港町。",
  "A domain consisting of the lands within the current-day Ibaraki Prefecture area. Its rulers comprised one of the Three Houses of the Tokugawa, although members of the Mito house were ineligible to become Shogun.": "現在の茨城県中部から北部を治めた藩。\n徳川御三家の一つである。",
  "A domain located in the south of Kyushu. The area is part of the current-day Kagoshima Prefecture.": "現在の鹿児島県の西部。",
  "Kawaraban": "瓦版",
  "Illustrations of a sexually arousing nature, including various forms of intercourse.": "男女の情交のさまを描いた絵。この頃、流行した\n性風俗を描いた浮世絵の一種。",
  "A newspaper with reports on recent events, often featuring detailed maps or other illustrations. Vendors sold these streetside, routinely announcing the latest headlines for passersby.": "町で起こった事件を絵入りで速報する情報紙。\n売り子が市中を売り歩く。",
  "High Goshi": "白札郷士",
  "Bon Dance": "盆踊り",
  "The traditional dance performed during the Bon festival, held in the middle of August in memory of those who have passed. The specific dance moves and accompanying music vary by region.": "盆（日本の８月中旬）に死者を供養するための行事、\nまたその行事内で行なわれる踊り。",
  "Meaning \"large\" or \"thick,\" this expression comes from a popular song in sumo jinku (sumo folk music). Wrestlers publicly perform these songs during special exhibitions and ceremonies.": "相撲甚句（すもうじんく）という相撲力士が\n歌う民謡の中で使われている。\n意味は“大きい”“太い”といった意味で、\n西日本の方言から来ている。",
  "Shinto Priest ": "神主",
  "Blessings of good fortune and favor received after doing work in the name of Buddha and the gods. ": "神仏を信ずることによって受ける恵み、幸運、恩恵。",
  "Known as \"kannushi\" in Japanese, these priests perform rituals dedicated to the Shinto gods while also maintaining their shrines' upkeep. ": "神道（日本の宗教）において、神に奉仕する人のこと。\n神様に捧げる“祭祀”を執り行ったり、\n神社の維持、管理を行う。",
  "Known as \"miko\" in Japanese, these women perform various duties at Shinto shrines. These include aiding in sacred rites, offering prayers, performing ceremonial songs and dances, and fortune-telling. They have also served more shamanistic roles during earlier periods of Japanese history.": "神道（日本の宗教）において、神に奉仕する女性のこと。\n神楽を舞ったり、祈祷、占いなどを行う。",
  "A nomadic monk in the Fuke sect of Zen Buddhism. Unlike other monks, instead of shaving their heads, they wear braided straw hats concealing their faces. Their practices include playing meditative shakuhachi solos in exchange for donations.": "禅宗の一派である“普化宗（ふけしゅう）”の僧。\n一般的な僧とは違い、頭を丸めておらず、編み笠を\nかぶっている。\n修行のため、尺八を吹きながら、諸国を行脚する。",
  "Representative": "筆頭",
  "Ishin": "維新",
  "Haori": "羽織",
  "Swordsmanship that utilizes the wakizashi (a spare katana, or a short sword).": "脇差（予備の刀、短刀）を使用する剣術。",
  "Dappan ": "脱藩",
  "A method of suicide initially practiced solely by samurai wherein one slices open one's own abdomen with a short sword.": "自らの腹部を短刀で切り裂いて死ぬ自殺の一方法。\n武士などが行った日本独特の習俗。",
  "A traditional style of dance. Unlike kabuki and noh, women were not prohibited from performing buyo.": "舞、踊りの総称。ダンス。",
  "Satsuma": "薩摩",
  "Term used when talking about both the Satsuma and Choshu Domains. ": "薩摩藩と長州藩のこと。",
  "Satcho ": "薩長",
  "Dutch Medicine ": "蘭方医",
  "Naval craft built in the Western world. The methods of their construction involved painting the hulls with black pitch, leading to impressionable, intimidating designs that greatly contrasted Japanese shipbuilding techniques.": "西洋からの船の事。\nこの頃来航した船の船体が黒で塗装されていたため、\n当時の日本でこう呼ばれた。",
  "Street Killing ": "辻斬り",
  "Dojo ": "道場",
  "Heyazumi ": "部屋住み",
  "Goshi": "郷士",
  "Chosokabe": "長宗我部",
  "Sekigahara": "関ヶ原",
  "The site of a decisive battle in 1600 that led to the informal rise of the Tokugawa shogunate. The site is now part of the current-day Gifu Prefecture.": "関ヶ原の戦い。西暦１６００年に\n関ヶ原（現在の岐阜県不群軍関ケ原町）を\n主戦場として行われた野戦。",
  "Awa": "阿波",
  "Black Ships": "黒船",
  "A faction within the Tokugawa family who fought for their candidate, Tokugawa Yoshinobu, to succeed the 13th Shogun.": "１３代将軍継嗣において、\n一橋徳川家の当主、徳川慶喜を推薦した一派。",
  "A faction within the Tokugawa family who fought for their candidate, Tokugawa Iemochi, to succeed the 13th Shogun.": "１３代将軍継嗣において、\n御三家の一つ紀州徳川家の当主、\n徳川家茂を推薦した一派。",
  "A two-year period of strife beginning in 1858 where the Bakufu used lethal and non-lethal methods to silence critics of Japan's international trade treaties.": "１８５８年、幕府に批判的な勢力を一掃するために\nおこなった弾圧事件。",
  "Mimawarigumi\nSasaki Tadasaburo": "京都見回り組\n佐々木只三郎",
  "Tosa Clan Magistrate\nYoshida Toyo": "土佐藩参政\n吉田東洋",
  "Tosa Samurai\nNakaoka Shintaro": "土佐藩士\n中岡慎太郎",
  "Bakufu Navy Admiral\nKatsu Rintaro": "幕府軍艦奉行並\n勝麟太郎",
  "Shinsengumi Seventh Division Captain\nTani Sanjuro": "新選組七番隊隊長\n谷三十郎",
  "Shinsengumi Ninth Division Captain\nSuzuki Mikisaburo": "新選組九番隊隊長\n鈴木三樹三郎",
  "Shinsengumi Fifth Division Captain\nTakeda Kanryusai": "新選組五番隊隊長\n武田観柳斎",
  "Shinsengumi Eighth Division Captain\nTodo Heisuke": "新選組八番隊隊長\n藤堂平助",
  "Shinsengumi Sixth Division Captain\nInoue Genzaburo": "新選組六番隊隊長\n井上源三郎",
  "Shinsengumi Advisor\nIto Kashitaro": "新選組参謀\n伊東甲子太郎",
  "Shinsengumi Fourth Division Captain\nMatsubara Chuji": "新選組四番隊隊長\n松原忠治",
  "Commander of the Satsuma Military\nSaigo Kichinosuke": "薩摩藩軍賦役\n西郷吉之助",
  "wepct9000": "wepct9000",
  "wepct8801": "wepct8801",
  "wepct8851": "wepct8851",
  "wepct8800": "wepct8800",
  "wepct8850": "wepct8850",
  "格闘": "格闘",
  "一刀": "一刀",
  "短銃": "短銃",
  "乱舞": "乱舞",
  "特殊武器": "特殊武器",
  "その他(配置武器など)": "その他(配置武器など)",
  "Disassemble the equipment you have on hand to obtain materials.": "手持ちの武具を使用して素材を入手します。",
  "Donate the equipment you have on hand to raise the level of Kurogane Smithing.": "手持ちの武具を使用して鍛冶屋のレベルを上げます。",
  "Craft new equipment according to their capabilities.": "武具派生を確認しながら、武具を作成します。",
  "Enhance your equipment with seals.": "手持ちの武具に印をはめて、強化します。",
  "Craft special ammunition.": "特殊な弾丸を作成します。",
  "About Kurogane Smithing.": "鍛冶屋についての説明です。",
  "You don't have enough hammers.": "金槌が足りません。",
  "Choose the type of equipment you wish to enhance.": "強化する武具の種類を選択してください。",
  "The cost to make this is {s_value}. Okay?": "作成費用は{s_value}です。よろしいですか？",
  "The cost to make this is {s_value}. Seals exceeding the number of slots in your new weapon will not be transferred.": "作成費用は{s_value}です。枠が足りない分の印は継承されません。",
  "The cost to fuse this is {s_value}. If you've got duplicate seals, the better one will stay.": "合成費用は{s_value}です。重複した印はいい色の印だけ残します。",
  "The cost to enhance this is {s_value}. Okay?": "強化費用は{s_value}です。よろしいですか？",
  "You don't have enough money.": "所持金が足りません。",
  "You don't have enough materials.": "素材が足りません。",
  "You don't have anything you can use to enhance this weapon.": "強化に使えるものがありません。",
  "Smithing level too low to enhance this equipment.": "これを作るには鍛冶屋レベルが足りません。",
  "I can't give this one any abilities yet. Bring the grade up to Good to gain a slot.": "これにはまだ能力を付与できません。\n良業物まで格上げすれば印の枠が増加します。",
  "You can't hold any more.": "これ以上持てません。",
  "This seal doesn't stack.": "２つ以上は効果を発揮しない印です。",
  "Enchanted weapons cannot be forged at Kurogane Smithing.": "妖刀の類はくろがね屋で作成できません。",
  "No seal selected.": "印が選択されていません。",
  "We're gonna fuse this with a new ability.": "「合成」を行い、武具に新しい能力を付与するぞ。",
  "We're gonna temper this to improve its defense.": "「鍛錬」を行い、武具の防御力を上昇させるぞ。",
  "We're gonna raise its grade by 1.": "「格上げ」を行い、武具の格を１つ上昇させるぞ。",
  "Select equipment to disassemble for materials.": "素材にする武具を選択してください。",
  "Select the equipment you'd like to make.": "作りたい武具を選択してください。",
  "Select the equipment you'd like to enhance.": "強化する武具を選択してください。"
 },
